\par
\b Project Summary\par\b0
I’m proposing a graduate-level Flutter application called \b Foodie\b0  — a “Tinder for Food” experience that helps students discover \b on-campus restaurants within walking distance\b0  through a swipe interface. The core loop is simple: I show one restaurant at a time with photos and key info; the user swipes right to “match” and save it into a local basket, or swipes left to discard it for the current session.\par
\par
This project is \b offline-first\b0  and follows the course rule of \b NO cloud-based storage\b0 . All restaurant data, menus, and demo ratings are mocked and stored locally (seeded into SQLite and/or bundled local assets). Settings are stored using SharedPreferences.\par
\par
\b Target Users\par\b0
Students who want quick, low-effort restaurant suggestions near campus, plus a saved “basket” of places they matched.\par
\par
\b Core Features (High-Level)\par\b0
\tab - On-campus restaurant discovery within a walking-distance radius (no GPS)\par
\tab - Swipe deck for restaurants (right = save match; left = discard session)\par
\tab - Restaurant detail view with menu, website link, and tap-to-call phone number\par
\tab - “Empty Basket” screen powered by SQLite (view/delete/clear)\par
\tab - Settings screen (dark mode, units, notifications toggle)\par
\tab - Graduate extras: background task + local notifications + export to file (JSON/CSV)\par
\par
\b Local Storage Plan (No Cloud)\par\b0
\tab - SQLite (sqflite): restaurants, menu items, matches (basket), and editable notes/reviews.\par
\tab - SharedPreferences: theme mode (dark/light), units (mi/km), notification toggle.\par
\tab - File system: export basket/reviews to documents directory as JSON/CSV.\par
\par
\b Architecture + State Management Intent (Graduate)\par\b0
I will use \b Clean Architecture\b0  with clear separation of Data / Domain / Presentation layers and the Repository pattern. For state management, I will use \b BLoC with Cubit (flutter_bloc)\b0  so UI updates are reactive and business rules remain testable and independent from widgets. Dependencies will be wired through \b get_it\b0  (dependency injection/service locator).\par
