\b Wireframe Plan Details\par\b0
Below is my wireframe plan (screens, transitions, and primary use cases). I’ll iterate on these screens with quick prototypes, user-flow checks, and test/refine cycles.\par
\par
\b Screen List (Minimum 5)\par\b0
1) \b Onboarding / Welcome\b0\par
\tab - Purpose: explain how the app works (swipe right/left), clarify it’s offline-first, and set an initial walking-distance radius (\b default: 2 miles\b0 ).\par
\tab - Edge cases: none for permissions (no GPS); handle empty data gracefully.\par
\tab - Transition: continue to Discover after onboarding is completed.\par
\par
2) \b Discover (Swipe Deck)\b0\par
\tab - Purpose: main swipe experience (restaurant cards).\par
\tab - Card content: building/exterior photo first; food photos in auto-advancing carousel; distance + estimated travel minutes.\par
\tab - Gestures: swipe right saves match; swipe left discards for session.\par
\tab - Transition: tap card to open Restaurant Details.\par
\par
3) \b Restaurant Details\b0\par
\tab - Purpose: deeper profile view.\par
\tab - Includes: menu (mocked/local), ratings (mocked/local), website link, tap-to-call.\par
\tab - Actions: add/edit a note/review (CRUD), optionally add/remove from basket.\par
\par
4) \b Basket\b0\par
\tab - Purpose: view matched restaurants saved in SQLite.\par
\tab - Actions: delete a single item, or “Empty Basket” to clear all (with explicit animation + confirmation dialog).\par
\tab - Transition: tap an item to open Restaurant Details.\par
\par
5) \b Settings\b0\par
\tab - Purpose: user preferences stored in SharedPreferences.\par
\tab - Toggles: dark mode, units (mi/km) or travel mode (walk/drive estimate), notifications on/off.\par
\par
\b Navigation & Transitions\par\b0
\tab - BottomNavigationBar for Discover / Basket / Settings.\par
\tab - Details screen pushed from Discover and Basket.\par
\tab - Onboarding shown first until the user completes/dismisses it.\par
\par
\b Data Flow (User Story Walkthrough)\par\b0
\tab 1) User opens app → onboarding explains the app + sets walking radius (default: 2 miles).\par
\tab 2) Discover loads restaurants from local SQLite seed → filters to the walking radius and shows distance/walk-time from a campus center.\par
\tab 3) User swipes right → app inserts BasketMatch into SQLite.\par
\tab 4) Basket screen reads matches from SQLite and displays them.\par
\tab 5) User taps “Empty Basket” → app deletes all BasketMatch rows → UI animates clearing.\par
\par
\b CRUD Evidence Plan (Required)\par\b0
\tab - Create: swipe-right inserts BasketMatch; add note inserts Review/Note.\par
\tab - Read: list restaurants; list basket; read menu + ratings in details.\par
\tab - Update: edit an existing review/note.\par
\tab - Delete: delete one basket item; delete all via Empty Basket.\par
\par
\b Graduate Advanced Features Plan\par\b0
\tab - Local notifications: daily/periodic reminder like “Today’s top pick.”\par
\tab - Background processing: schedule a task that selects the day’s pick from local history.\par
\tab - File system: export basket/reviews to JSON/CSV.\par
\tab - Animations: explicit swipe transitions + explicit “empty basket” animation.\par
\par
\b Testing Plan (Graduate)\par\b0
\tab - Unit tests (10+): domain use cases, cubits, validation logic.\par
\tab - Widget tests: swipe deck interaction + basket empty flow.\par
\tab - Integration test: swipe-right persists, then appears in basket on next launch.\par
\tab - Coverage: provide command and output via flutter test --coverage.\par
\par
\b Version Control + Execution Plan\par\b0
I will maintain steady progress in GitHub with small, meaningful commits and feature branches. My goal is at least \b 20+ commits per contributor\b0  with clear commit messages, plus pull requests for major features. This will make the work easy to review and aligns with the course’s commit activity enforcement.\par
}
